      "message": "Marco, Jerome:\n\nThis CL and the [follow-up CL](https://aomedia-review.googlesource.com/c/aom/+/200061) modified the `aom_roi_map_t` struct in the public header. In general a change to a public type breaks backward compatibility. However, since the `AOME_SET_ROI_MAP` codec control was unimplemented, no libaom clients could use the `aom_roi_map_t` struct successfully. So we should be able to make an exception and allow this. I will discuss this issue with James.",
